IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-interpretation-time`

-- Part V of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Powers, functions and authorities, sections 39 to 48B.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- Section 40(1) counts "1 year after" a day with the time module (section 28(1)).
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no, and NOTHING where it does not.

§ `Section 39: confirmation of appointments not required`

-- An appointment or other exercise of a power does not cease to have effect or need to be confirmed by reason only that the person making it has ceased to hold office or to be capable of exercising the power.
-- src:600 | An appointment or other exercise of a power does not cease to have effect or need to be confirmed by reason only that the person making the appointment or exercising the power has ceased to hold office or otherwise to be capable of exercising the power.
@ref s 39 (src:600)
GIVEN `the only reason is that the person making the appointment or exercising the power has ceased to hold office or otherwise to be capable of exercising the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39: the appointment or exercise of the power ceases to have effect or needs to be confirmed` MEANS
    IF   `the only reason is that the person making the appointment or exercising the power has ceased to hold office or otherwise to be capable of exercising the power`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 40: continuing to act during a vacancy`

-- A person acting in an office during the absence or inability of the office-holder may, if the office-holder ceases to hold the office, continue to act until the earlier of
-- the lawful revocation of the person's authority to act and 1 year after the office-holder ceased to hold office.
-- The last day on which the person may act is the earlier of the day of revocation and the last day of the 1 year counted from the day after the office-holder ceased (section 28(1)).
-- src:602 | (1) If a person is acting in an office (including a Ministerial office) during the absence or inability of the office-holder and, for any reason, the office-holder ceases to hold the office, the person acting may continue to act in the office until the earlier of the following:
-- src:603 | (a) the lawful revocation of the person's authority to act;
-- src:604 | (b) 1 year after the office-holder ceased to hold office.
@ref s 40(1) (src:602-604)
GIVEN `the day on which the office-holder ceased to hold office` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person's authority to act is lawfully revoked, if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 40(1): the last day on which the person acting may continue to act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` `the day on which the office-holder ceased to hold office` 1 `years`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `end of the year` THEN
        CONSIDER `the day on which the person's authority to act is lawfully revoked, if it is`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `end of the year`
        WHEN JUST revoked THEN
            IF   Day revoked LESS THAN Day `end of the year`
            THEN JUST revoked
            ELSE JUST `end of the year`

-- Acting in an office includes performing the duties of the office.
-- src:606 | acting in an office includes performing the duties of the office.
@ref s 40(2) "acting in an office" (src:606)
GIVEN `the person is performing the duties of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2) "acting in an office": the person is acting in the office` MEANS
    IF `the person is performing the duties of the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Office includes a position and a designation.
-- src:607 | office includes a position and a designation.
@ref s 40(2) "office" (src:607)
GIVEN `it is a position or a designation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2) "office": the thing is an office` MEANS
    IF `it is a position or a designation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 41: occasions for exercise of powers`

-- Where an Act confers a power or imposes a duty, the power may be exercised and the duty performed from time to time as occasion requires.
-- src:609 | (1) Where an Act confers a power or imposes a duty, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref s 41(1) (src:609)
GIVEN `occasion requires it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(1): the power may be exercised and the duty performed on the occasion` MEANS
    IF `occasion requires it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Where an Act confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office, or the occupier of a position or designation, as such,
-- the power may be exercised and the duty performed by the person for the time being holding, occupying or performing the duties of it.
-- src:610 | (2) Where an Act confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office or the occupier of a position or designation as such, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the person for the time being holding or occupying or performing the duties of the office, position or designation.
@ref s 41(2) (src:610)
GIVEN `the power or duty is conferred on the holder of an office or the occupier of a position or designation as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person for the time being holds, occupies or performs the duties of the office, position or designation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(2): the person may exercise the power and must perform the duty` MEANS
    IF   `the power or duty is conferred on the holder of an office or the occupier of a position or designation as such`
         AND `the person for the time being holds, occupies or performs the duties of the office, position or designation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 42 to 44A: how powers may be exercised`

DECLARE `Manner of exercising a power to make an instrument` IS ONE OF
    `in whole or in part`
    `so that it is subject to conditions, limitations or qualifications specified in the instrument`
    `to make different provision in relation to different matters or classes of matters`
    `to apply differently by reference to exceptions or factors specified in the instrument`
    `in some other manner`

-- A power to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument may be exercised in the four ways listed.
-- src:612 | (1) A power under an Act to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument may be exercised:
-- src:613 | (a) in whole or in part;
-- src:614 | (b) so that it is subject to any conditions, limitations or qualifications specified in the instrument;
-- src:615 | (c) to make different provision in relation to different matters or classes of matters; or
-- src:616 | (d) to apply differently by reference to exceptions or factors specified in the instrument.
@ref s 42(1) (src:612-616)
GIVEN manner IS A `Manner of exercising a power to make an instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(1): the power to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument may be exercised in that manner` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `in some other manner` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The power is not limited to a particular matter merely because the Act makes provision in relation to another matter.
-- src:617 | (2) The power is not limited to making provision in relation to a particular matter or a particular aspect of a matter merely because the Act makes provision in relation to another matter or another aspect of the matter.
@ref s 42(2) (src:617)
GIVEN `the only reason is that the Act makes provision in relation to another matter or another aspect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(2): the power is limited to a particular matter or aspect of a matter` MEANS
    IF `the only reason is that the Act makes provision in relation to another matter or another aspect of the matter` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 42 applies to a power whether exercised before or after the commencement of the section.
-- The text has no subsection (3) (the printed numbers run (1), (2), (4)).
-- src:618 | (4) This section applies in relation to a power whether exercised before or after the commencement of this section.
@ref s 42(4) (src:618)
GIVEN `the power was exercised before the commencement of section 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(4): section 42 applies in relation to the power` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the power was exercised before the commencement of section 42`
    WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE

-- A power to take an action, or to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument, includes a power to repeal, rescind, revoke, amend or vary the action or instrument.
-- src:620 | A power under an Act to take an action or to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument includes a power, exercisable in the same manner and subject to the same conditions, to repeal, rescind, revoke, amend or vary the action or instrument.
@ref s 43 (src:620)
GIVEN `what is done to the action or instrument` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43: the power includes the power to do the thing to the action or instrument, in the same manner and subject to the same conditions` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN known YIELD known EQUALS `what is done to the action or instrument`) (LIST "repeal", "rescind", "revoke", "amend", "vary")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subject to subsection (3), a power to make appointments to an office or position includes a power to terminate an appointment, or to remove or suspend a person appointed.
-- src:622 | (1) Subject to subsection (3), where an Act confers on any person or authority a power to make appointments to any office or position, the power shall be construed as including a power to terminate such an appointment or to remove or suspend any person appointed.
@ref s 44(1) (src:622)
GIVEN `what is done to the person appointed` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(1): the power to make appointments includes the power to do the thing to the person appointed` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN known YIELD known EQUALS `what is done to the person appointed`) (LIST "terminate the appointment", "remove", "suspend")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Where the power to appoint is exercisable only on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of some other person or authority,
-- the power of termination or removal is exercisable only on that recommendation, approval or consent.
-- src:623 | (3) Where a power to make appointments to an office or position is exercisable only upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of some other person or authority, the power of termination or removal referred to in subsection (1) is exercisable only upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of that other person or authority.
@ref s 44(3) (src:623)
GIVEN `the power to appoint is exercisable only upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of some other person or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the termination or removal has that recommendation, approval or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(3): the power of termination or removal may be exercised` MEANS
    IF   `the power to appoint is exercisable only upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of some other person or authority`
    THEN JUST `the termination or removal has that recommendation, approval or consent`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- If an Act authorises or requires an appointer to appoint a person to an office or position, the appointer may appoint one or more people to act during a vacancy or a period when the holder is unable to perform the duties.
-- src:625 | If an Act authorises or requires a person or authority (the appointer) to appoint a person to an office or position, the appointer may appoint a person, or 2 or more people, to act in the office or position:
-- src:626 | (a) during a vacancy, or all vacancies, in the office or position whether or not an appointment has previously been made to the office or position; or
-- src:627 | (b) during any period, or all periods, when the holder of the office or position is unable to perform the duties of the office or position.
@ref s 44A (src:625-627)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires the appointer to appoint a person to the office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is to act during a vacancy in the office or position, whether or not an appointment has previously been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is to act during a period when the holder of the office or position is unable to perform the duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A: the appointer may appoint a person, or 2 or more people, to act` MEANS
    IF   `an Act authorises or requires the appointer to appoint a person to the office or position`
         AND (`the appointment is to act during a vacancy in the office or position, whether or not an appointment has previously been made`
              OR `the appointment is to act during a period when the holder of the office or position is unable to perform the duties`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 46 and 46A: authorising another person and delegation`

DECLARE `Way of naming the person on whom authority is conferred` IS ONE OF
    `a person by name`
    `a person by reference to the office, position or designation held or occupied by the person`
    `a person from time to time holding, acting in or performing the duties of a named office, designation or position`
    `a person in some other way`

-- Authority may be conferred on a person by name, by the office, position or designation held, or on whoever from time to time holds, acts in or performs the duties of a named office.
-- src:635 | (3) Authority may be conferred pursuant to subsection (1) on:
-- src:636 | (a) a person by name;
-- src:637 | (b) a person by reference to the office, position or designation held or occupied by the person; or
-- src:638 | (c) a person from time to time holding, acting in or performing the duties of a named office, designation or position.
@ref s 46(3) (src:635-638)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of naming the person on whom authority is conferred`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(3): authority may be conferred on a person in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `a person in some other way` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 46 does not apply to a function or power of a legislative or judicial nature, or relating to the investigation or detection of offences or other unlawful acts,
-- or relating to the grant, defeasance or forfeiture of a right or title to land.
-- src:641 | (7) This section does not apply to:
-- src:642 | (a) a function or power of a legislative or judicial nature; or
-- src:643 | (b) a function or power relating to:
-- src:644 | (i) the investigation or detection of offences or other unlawful acts; or
-- src:645 | (ii) the grant or the defeasance or forfeiture of a right or title to land.
@ref s 46(7) (src:641-645)
GIVEN `the function or power is of a legislative or judicial nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function or power relates to the investigation or detection of offences or other unlawful acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function or power relates to the grant or the defeasance or forfeiture of a right or title to land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(7): section 46 applies to the function or power` MEANS
    IF   `the function or power is of a legislative or judicial nature`
         OR `the function or power relates to the investigation or detection of offences or other unlawful acts`
         OR `the function or power relates to the grant or the defeasance or forfeiture of a right or title to land`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- A function or power conferred on a minister may be performed by a person who has the minister's authority;
-- one conferred on another person may be performed by a person who, with the approval of the minister administering the provision (or of someone that minister authorises to give it), has the authority of the person on whom it is conferred.
-- Subsection (1) does not empower the exercise of a power by authority that is not evidenced in a written instrument.
-- src:629 | (1) If an Act or a statutory instrument confers a function or power on a minister or other person (whether by reference to an office or otherwise), the function or power may be performed or exercised:
-- src:630 | (a) for a minister – by a person who has the authority of the minister; or
-- src:631 | (b) otherwise – by a person who, with the approval of the minister administering the provision conferring the function or power, or of a person authorised by that minister to give that approval, has the authority of the person on whom the function or power is conferred.
-- src:632 | Note for subsection (1)
-- src:633 | See subsection (7) for functions and powers to which this section does not apply.
-- src:634 | (2) Subsection (1) does not empower the exercise of a power or the performance of a function by the authority of a person where that authority is not evidenced in a written instrument.
@ref s 46(1), (2) (src:629-634)
GIVEN `section 46 applies to the function or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function or power is conferred on a minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the authority of the minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the authority of the person on whom the function or power is conferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that authority was given with the approval of the minister administering the provision, or of a person authorised by that minister to give the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is evidenced in a written instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(1), (2): the person may perform the function or exercise the power by authority` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `section 46 applies to the function or power`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   (NOT `the authority is evidenced in a written instrument`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF   `the function or power is conferred on a minister`
              THEN JUST `the person has the authority of the minister`
              ELSE JUST (`the person has the authority of the person on whom the function or power is conferred`
                         AND `that authority was given with the approval of the minister administering the provision, or of a person authorised by that minister to give the approval`)

DECLARE `Person who might exercise a power after authority is conferred` IS ONE OF
    `the person conferring the authority`
    `another person on whom authority to exercise the power or perform the function is conferred`
    `anyone else`

-- The conferring of authority does not prevent the exercise of the power by the person conferring it or by another person on whom authority is conferred.
-- src:639 | (5) The conferring of authority by an instrument under this section does not prevent the exercise of the power or the performance of the function by the person conferring the authority or by another person on whom authority to exercise the power or perform the function is conferred.
@ref s 46(5) (src:639)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who might exercise a power after authority is conferred`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(5): the conferring of authority prevents the person from exercising the power` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- The performance of a function or exercise of a power by authority is subject to conditions and limitations specified in the instrument conferring the authority.
-- src:640 | (6) The performance of a function or exercise of a power by the authority of a person under this section is subject to any conditions and limitations specified in the instrument conferring the authority.
@ref s 46(6) (src:640)
GIVEN `the instrument specifies conditions or limitations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the performance or exercise keeps within them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(6): the performance or exercise is within the authority conferred` MEANS
    IF `the instrument specifies conditions or limitations` THEN JUST `the performance or exercise keeps within them` ELSE NOTHING

-- A power to delegate a power or function is construed as a power to delegate to a person by name, by office, position or designation, or to whoever from time to time holds, acts in or performs the duties of a named office.
-- src:647 | (1) A provision of an Act that confers a power to delegate a power or function on a person (whether by reference to an office, designation, position or otherwise) is to be construed as conferring on the person a power to delegate the power or function to:
-- src:648 | (a) a person by name;
-- src:649 | (b) a person by reference to the office, position or designation held or occupied by the person; or
-- src:650 | (c) a person from time to time holding, acting in or performing the duties of a named office, designation or position.
@ref s 46A(1) (src:647-650)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of naming the person on whom authority is conferred`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46A(1): the power to delegate may be exercised by delegating to a person in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `a person in some other way` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- A power to delegate is not construed as including the power to delegate that power of delegation.
-- src:651 | (2) A provision of an Act that confers a power to delegate a power or function is not to be construed as including the power to delegate that power of delegation.
@ref s 46A(2) (src:651)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act confers a power to delegate a power or function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46A(2): the power to delegate includes the power to delegate that power of delegation` MEANS
    IF `a provision of an Act confers a power to delegate a power or function` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- A power or function exercised or performed by the delegate is taken to be exercised or performed by the person who delegated it.
-- src:652 | (3) If a power or function is delegated under an Act, the power or function is, when exercised or performed by the delegate, to be taken to be exercised or performed by the person who delegated it.
@ref s 46A(3) (src:652)
GIVEN `the person who delegated the power or function` IS A STRING
      `the delegate is exercising the power or performing the function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 46A(3): the person by whom the power or function is taken to be exercised or performed` MEANS
    IF `the delegate is exercising the power or performing the function` THEN JUST `the person who delegated the power or function` ELSE NOTHING

-- The delegation of a power or function does not prevent its exercise or performance by the person who delegated it.
-- src:653 | (4) The delegation of the power or function under an Act does not prevent the exercise of the power or the performance of the function by the person who delegated it.
@ref s 46A(4) (src:653)
GIVEN `the power or function is delegated under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46A(4): the delegation prevents the person who delegated from exercising the power or performing the function` MEANS
    IF `the power or function is delegated under an Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 48 to 48B: discretions, meetings and minor errors`

-- Where the exercise of a power depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of a person, a delegate or a person authorised by that person may exercise it upon the delegate's or authorised person's own opinion, belief or state of mind.
-- src:655 | Where, under an Act, the exercise of a power or the performance of a function by a person is dependent upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of that person in relation to a matter, that power may be exercised or that function may be performed by a delegate or by authority of that person upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of the delegate or authorized person in relation to that matter.
@ref s 48 (src:655)
GIVEN `the exercise of the power or performance of the function depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is exercised or performed by a delegate or by authority of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48: the power may be exercised upon the opinion, belief or state of mind of the delegate or authorised person` MEANS
    IF   `the exercise of the power or performance of the function depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person`
         AND `it is exercised or performed by a delegate or by authority of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 48A applies to a body established by an Act if the Act requires or permits meetings of the members.
-- src:657 | (1) This section applies to a body (whether or not incorporated) established by an Act if the Act requires or permits meetings of the members of the body to be held.
@ref s 48A(1) (src:657)
GIVEN `the body (whether or not incorporated) is established by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act requires or permits meetings of the members of the body to be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(1): section 48A applies to the body` MEANS
    JUST (`the body (whether or not incorporated) is established by an Act` AND `the Act requires or permits meetings of the members of the body to be held`)

-- The body may permit its members to participate in a meeting by telephone, exchange of emails, online facilities or any other means of communication.
-- src:658 | (2) The body may permit its members to participate in a meeting or all meetings by:
-- src:659 | (a) telephone; or
-- src:660 | (b) exchange of emails; or
-- src:661 | (c) online facilities; or
-- src:662 | (d) any other means of communication.
@ref s 48A(2) (src:658-662)
GIVEN `section 48A applies to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(2): the body may permit its members to participate in a meeting by any means of communication` MEANS
    IF `section 48A applies to the body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- A member who participates in a meeting under such a permission is taken to be present at the meeting.
-- src:663 | (3) A member who participates in a meeting under a permission under subsection (2) is taken to be present at the meeting.
@ref s 48A(3) (src:663)
GIVEN `the body has permitted participation by that means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member participates in the meeting under the permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A(3): the member is taken to be present at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the body has permitted participation by that means` AND `the member participates in the meeting under the permission` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Error in a decision` IS ONE OF
    `a clerical mistake`
    `an error arising from an accidental slip or omission`
    `a material miscalculation of figures or a material mistake in the description of a person, thing or matter referred to in the decision`
    `a defect of form`
    `some other error`

DECLARE `How a correction is started` IS ONE OF
    `of the decision maker's own motion`
    `on application by a party to the proceeding`
    `in a way not named`

-- A decision made in proceedings before a person or body authorised to hear and determine a matter, that contains one of the four kinds of error, may be corrected by the decision maker
-- of the decision maker's own motion or on application by a party.
-- src:665 | (1) Where a decision made in proceedings before a person or body authorised by or under an Act to hear and determine a matter contains:
-- src:666 | (a) a clerical mistake;
-- src:667 | (b) an error arising from an accidental slip or omission;
-- src:668 | (c) a material miscalculation of figures or a material mistake in the description of a person, thing or matter referred to in the decision; or
-- src:669 | (d) a defect of form,
-- src:670 | the decision maker, of his or her own motion or on application by a party to the proceeding, may correct the decision.
@ref s 48B(1) (src:665-670)
GIVEN `the decision is made in proceedings before a person or body authorised by or under an Act to hear and determine a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      error IS A `Error in a decision`
      start IS A `How a correction is started`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(1): the decision maker may correct the decision` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `the decision is made in proceedings before a person or body authorised by or under an Act to hear and determine a matter`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER error
         WHEN `some other error` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE CONSIDER start
                   WHEN `in a way not named` THEN NOTHING
                   OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Thing that may be called a decision` IS ONE OF
    `a judgment`
    `an order`
    `a determination`
    `the reasons for a decision`
    `something other than a judgment, order, determination or reasons`

-- In section 48B, decision includes a judgment, order and determination, and the reasons for a decision.
-- src:671 | (2) In this section decision includes a judgment, order and determination, and the reasons for a decision.
@ref s 48B(2) (src:671)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that may be called a decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48B(2): the thing is a decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `something other than a judgment, order, determination or reasons` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
